Description: include NetAddress from the V\OS header layout
 The packaged include path adds the os/ tree but not its net/ subdirectory
 (vos.specs has no -I for os/net), so the legacy top-level <NetAddress.h>
 include does not resolve. V\OS ships the header at net/NetAddress.h;
 the app only pulls it in and never names BNetAddress, so this is a path
 fix and nothing else.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

---
--- a/Application/BeTrisApp.h
+++ b/Application/BeTrisApp.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #include <Application.h>
 #include <List.h>
 #include <String.h>
-#include <NetAddress.h>
+#include <net/NetAddress.h>
 #include <Path.h>
 #include <Resources.h>
 
